---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base
  title="Terms — Clicker"
  description="Plain-language terms for the Clicker website, app, plans, and beta."
>
  <article class="container prose">
    <p class="ecp">terms</p>
    <h1>Terms</h1>
    <p class="updated">Last updated: November 14, 2026</p>

    <h2>This site</h2>
    <p>
      This website is provided as-is, for information about the Clicker app
      and for requesting a beta invite. We may change or take down any part of
      it at any time.
    </p>

    <h2>The beta</h2>
    <p>
      Beta builds are distributed through Apple’s TestFlight and are covered
      by Apple’s TestFlight terms. Beta software is unfinished by definition:
      it may have bugs, and features may change or disappear before release.
      Requesting an invite doesn’t guarantee one — spots open in small
      batches.
    </p>

    <h2>The app</h2>
    <p>
      Clicker controls Roku devices using Roku’s openly documented External
      Control Protocol over your local network. You’re responsible for using
      it only with devices you’re allowed to control. Your use of the app is
      also covered by Apple’s standard end user license agreement for App
      Store apps.
    </p>

    <h2>Plans and payment</h2>
    <p>
      You can try the remote before paying. To keep using it you choose one
      of two plans, and each unlocks the whole app. The price of each is
      shown in the app before you buy, and may differ by country.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Weekly plan.</strong> This is an auto-renewing subscription
      billed to your Apple ID. If a free trial is offered, it lasts 3 days
      and then becomes a paid subscription. The plan renews every week at
      the price shown unless you cancel at least 24 hours before the current
      period ends. If the price ever goes up, Apple will tell you before it
      applies to you.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Cancelling.</strong> Cancel any time on your iPhone in
      Settings, under your name, in Subscriptions. Deleting the app does not
      cancel a subscription. After you cancel, the plan stays active until
      the end of the period you have paid for.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Lifetime plan.</strong> This is one payment that never renews.
      “Lifetime” means the life of the app: for as long as Clicker is offered
      and is able to control Roku devices. If you buy lifetime while a weekly
      plan is still running, cancel the weekly plan yourself, because Apple
      does not cancel it for you.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Refunds.</strong> Apple handles all payments and refunds. To
      ask for one, use
      <a href="https://reportaproblem.apple.com" rel="noopener">reportaproblem.apple.com</a>.
      We cannot issue refunds or cancel a subscription on your behalf.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>What a plan depends on.</strong> Clicker works by talking to
      your Roku over your own Wi-Fi. It relies on Roku’s software and on your
      network allowing your phone and Roku to reach each other, and either
      can change in ways we don’t control. If Clicker stops working for you,
      cancel the weekly plan so you are not charged again.
    </p>

    <h2>No warranty</h2>
    <p>
      To the maximum extent permitted by law, the site, the app, and the
      beta are provided without warranties of any kind, and we’re not liable
      for damages arising from their use.
    </p>

    <h2>Trademarks</h2>
    <p>
      Clicker is an independent project. It is not affiliated with or endorsed
      by Roku, Inc. Roku is a trademark of Roku, Inc. Apple, TestFlight, and
      App Store are trademarks of Apple Inc.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      <!-- TODO(domain): publish a contact address once the new domain and
           its email exist. -->
      A contact address will be published here when the site goes live.
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .prose {
    max-width: 680px;
    padding-block: calc(var(--space) * 10);
  }

  .prose h1 { margin-top: calc(var(--space) * 3); }

  .prose .updated {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 13px;
    color: var(--ink-faint);
    margin-top: var(--space);
  }

  .prose h2 {
    font-size: 24px;
    margin-top: calc(var(--space) * 5);
    margin-bottom: calc(var(--space) * 1.5);
  }

  .prose p + p { margin-top: calc(var(--space) * 2); }
</style>
